---
/**
 * The privacy policy. Every claim here is one the code actually keeps, so this
 * file and the app have to change together.
 *
 * Play requires a policy that names the Accessibility Service and says what it
 * is for, because an app that uses one without explaining it is removed.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Scrollsy collects, what it never sees, and who else is involved."
>
  <h1 class="headline">Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="fine">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <div class="doc">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Scrollsy counts how many reels you scroll. It counts that a reel went past.
      It never sees what the reel was.
    </p>

    <h2>How the counting works</h2>
    <p>
      Android has no other way to know a reel went past, so Scrollsy uses an
      Accessibility Service. It is limited to five apps, Instagram, TikTok,
      YouTube, Snapchat and the TikTok international build, and it is allowed to
      receive one kind of event, a scroll.
    </p>
    <p>
      It cannot read the screen. The permission that would let it do that is
      switched off in the service's own configuration, so no text, image, video,
      caption, message or account name from those apps is ever available to
      Scrollsy, even in memory.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is recorded is a number, and which of the five apps it happened in.
      Nothing else about the session is kept.
    </p>

    <h2>What Scrollsy stores about you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Google account id, name, email and profile photo, from signing in.</li>
      <li>Your daily reel counts, per app, per day.</li>
      <li>Which onboarding step you reached, so a new phone resumes where you stopped.</li>
      <li>Who you are friends with, when you or they accept an invite.</li>
      <li>Your settings, such as your daily limit and the counter style.</li>
      <li>Whether you have a paid plan, and when it runs out.</li>
      <li>Feedback you send, which is only what you typed and the topic you picked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What Scrollsy never stores</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Anything you watched, read, typed or sent in another app.</li>
      <li>Your contacts, photos, location, microphone or camera.</li>
      <li>Your card details. The store handles payment and Scrollsy never sees it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who else is involved</h2>
    <p>
      Google, for signing in. Supabase, which hosts the database. Cloudflare,
      which runs the server the app talks to. RevenueCat and Google Play, for
      subscriptions. Each one only receives what it needs to do its job.
    </p>
    <p>Scrollsy does not sell your data, and does not use it for advertising.</p>

    <h2>Friends see very little</h2>
    <p>
      Someone you are in a battle with sees your name, your photo and your reel
      count for the day. They never see your email, your settings, or anything
      about which apps the count came from.
    </p>

    <h2>Turning it off</h2>
    <p>
      You can switch off reel counting, the floating counter, or notifications at
      any time in Android settings, and the app keeps working without them. It
      just stops counting.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting everything</h2>
    <p>
      Settings has a delete account button. It removes your account, your counts,
      your friendships and your feedback. It does not cancel a subscription,
      because that lives with Google Play, and the app tells you so before you
      confirm.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about any of this can go to the feedback form inside the app,
      under Settings.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
  .doc {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.2px;
  }

  .doc p,
  .doc li {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 23px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .doc ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
